In Activity 5, I chose Gemini as my AI tool to explore image generation using different levels of prompt details.

For my first attempt, I used a simple prompt, which was 'Make a photo of a birthday party.' Gemini generated an indoor birthday celebration with friends. Although the image was good, it was different from what I originally imagined.

For my second attempt, I added more specific details. I instructed Gemini to create a lavish beach birthday party with a private chef, DJ, photo booth, and yacht. The result was closer to what I wanted because I provided clearer instructions.

Through this activity, I learned that the quality of our prompts affects the output generated by AI. We should be specific about the environment, objects, and details we want to include. This will help us get results that are closer to our expectations.

Activity 5 is not simply about generating beautiful pictures. It is about learning how to communicate effectively with AI through prompt engineering. The main difference between your first and second attempts is the level of detail in your instructions.
